# Landing visual refinement guardrails

- Treat the Landing as a **tennis intelligence system**, not a generic AI chatbot.
- Preserve the five canonical ideas: tennis lifecycle, multiple engines, multiple depths of use, evidence, real-match proof.
- Keep STRATEGIST and EXPLORER visibly distinct: `what we know -> plan` vs `what we do not know -> test -> learn`.
- Preserve Tour Manager and Player & Club Intelligence as separate capabilities; do not rename them into generic Agents.
- Preserve Quick / Detailed / Tracked as three distinct interaction depths.
- Tracked must retain a visible gesture/hand affordance slot.
- Preserve the living system graph and its data-driven model; do not revert to the old fixed linear SVG flow.
- Preserve app lifecycle media slots: pre-match, live, tracked-live, post-match.
- Preserve Real Match Proof as `what happened -> Explorer -> Strategist -> player adherence`.
- Never expose OpenHands, model/provider names, secrets, internal prompts, protected evaluation logic or hidden reasoning in customer copy.
- Keep IT/EN, mobile-first reading order, keyboard accessibility, reduced motion and safe DOM rendering.
- CRISP remains support transport; native TennisAgents AI remains the product conversation surface.
- Do not mutate Production, main, shared TEST or release gates from Design Mode.
- After visual edits run Landing quality, system-story, persistent-AI and visual-review checks.

